# Scene
trueqbit with Claude (Opus 5.5), 2026-11-21: the released names of the
config macro review.

# Decided
- 9 language features -> SQLITE_ORM_CPP_<F>_SUPPORTED, no aliases (trueqbit:
  reporting the compiler's language support is not sqlite_orm's concern).
- CPP20_CONCEPTS -> CPP20_LIB_CONCEPTS, CPP20_RANGES -> CPP20_LIB_RANGES,
  STL_HAS_DEFAULT_SENTINEL -> CPP20_LIB_DEFAULT_SENTINEL_SUPPORTED, no aliases
  for now.
- SQLITE_ORM_OMITS_CODECVT -> SQLITE_ORM_OMIT_CODECVT with a deprecated alias
  (trueqbit: a real public contract). CMake: only option(SQLITE_ORM_OMIT_CODECVT);
  the old name from -D or a cache gives message(DEPRECATION) and sets the new
  one; capabilities.h maps the old macro for projects defining it by hand.
- The tier preambles state the naming as a pattern after the standard's
  prefixes __cpp_ / __cpp_lib_ - not one-to-one: DEDUCING_THIS,
  DEFAULT_COMPARISONS, INITSTMT_RANGE_BASED_FOR, DEFAULT_SENTINEL differ.
- trueqbit: the commit leaves the open alias question to the record and the
  pull request; it would be stale as a stated state.

# Discussed
- Checks: -E -dM of both published headers through the full mapping
  identical (C++17/20/26, g++-16, clang++); the alias in all four
  combinations; CMake 4.4.1 configure of a wrapper project: none -> no
  definition, new -> =1, old -> deprecation + =1, old removed from cache ->
  none.

